passt: let the kernel pick the host source port of outbound UDP

`--no-udp-port-keep`: for a UDP flow the guest starts, the host side gets a
port the kernel picks, as passt already does for TCP (`fwd.c`,
`fwd_nat_from_tap`). Without it the host side binds the guest's own source
port, with SO_REUSEADDR (`util.c`).

pynixd runs one passt per build VM, and every guest runs the same kernel.
Two guests that use the same source port to reach one resolver bind the
same host port in two passt processes, and the replies reach only one of
them. Measured on dynhetz, 100 build VMs at once, 5000 lookups each run:
7, 3, 1 and 1 lookups failed with EAI_AGAIN after both of glibc's 5 s
attempts; passt's --pcap showed those queries with no reply, from ports two
concurrent guests shared. On the host's own namespaces: 0 of 5000.

`udp_flow_new` reads the port back with getsockname when the kernel picked
it, as it does for an address the kernel picked.

To report upstream (passt.top), once pynixd has measured it.

