 .TP
+.BR \-\-no-udp-port-keep
+For a UDP flow the guest or namespace starts, let the kernel pick the host
+side source port, as for TCP. By default, the host side keeps the guest's
+source port. Two instances whose guests use the same source port to reach
+the same destination then bind the same host port, and the replies reach
+only one of them. Use this when several instances run on one host, each
+with its own guest, as build sandboxes do.
+
+.TP
 .BR \-\-map-host-loopback " " \fIaddr
 Translate \fIaddr\fR to refer to the host. Packets from the guest to
 \fIaddr\fR will be redirected to the host.  On the host such packets
